When I sat down last night, I picked up the wrong laptop, and had a game
started before I realized that.  So I continued.  Until almost 2 :) But
more of that in a bit.

This morning while transferring 100M to a zip disk, I pulled it out.
Everything near me, save the werething when an @, would respect the E
word.  I still had 56 hp, so I figured I'd E and then grab a scroll from
the bag.  Foolishly, I tried 3 or 4 times, as it didn't work.  I had
enough HP that I *should* have just grabbed the scroll of fortress and
taken the hit.  *sigh*

Or I could have broke a wand of forcebolt (though I had no guarantee it
had any charges, but there were 5).

Oh, well.

But the wizard on the new laptop is thriving, save for the lack of a
decent attack spell (sleep & forcebolt only).  There were plenty of
early potions, and then he found a double-bones on the Oracle.  One from
a wizard who had apparently put down his bag of holding to move statues
(and died carrying two when a mumak was generated on the next square.
Argh.  So much for out of sight).  So lots of potions & scrolls, and he
even started with a wand of cancellation to blank them with.

You can see where this is going?

Sting obnoxiously showed up randomly generated at the top of sokoban,
but it was at least as good as the runed dager he was using.

Blessed the bag and a couple of luckstones and two of the three magic
lamps at Iczaaks.  (silver +3 and speed boots).

Went to apply B to take something out of the bag of holding.  Huh?  Oh,
and no wand, either . . . *sigh* . . . at least the spellbooks were
safely stashed away, but they keep repeating.

So now he has the still unenchanted magicbane, and got handed Ogresmash
(gee, thanks).  Mines End was the library, but didn't get much useful
there (though I later found a charm monster).  Noctus, the starting cat,
got turned into a Jabberwok down there.  I forgot they could open doors.
Sorry, I.  . . .

And now for the part that people read my posts for . . .

The adrenalin surge as I realized that I'd just moved blind onto the
square where I'd killed a cockatrice.  Hmm, nice gloves.  I didn't think
they saved you blind . . .

I accidentally bumped the minetown priestess (co-aligned, at that).  Oops,
she won't be much use to me much more (I'm still not sure how I bumped
her; maybe tossing away an excess corpse.)  So I tried to get noctus to
take care of her and get a refund.  No dice.  Many tries, and he
wouldn't go in.  I even knocked a few holes in the wall, but still no.

And then I managed to bump her again, and got lightning from my angry
god.  Oh, dear.  This isn't good.  In fact, this could be bad, having
blown up all my food and having several levels to trek . . .

Noctus still didn't go in.

Then I remembered something I heard.  Gee, charm monster works great;
she was happy again.

So noctus went in and killed her.  

Oh, well.  Between that and A couple of merchants, I'm now fully
protected from a chaotic priestess.

Noctus got lost along the way; I even went all the way to 1 looking when
went back to sokoban to reread spells.  But I've found him; he found the
quest portal, and it only took 4 or 5 tries to retame him.   Hmm, two
more levels and I can do the quest.  

